  "validity_note": "CoolProp's incompressible aqueous ethanol correlation (INCOMP::MEA), built on Melinder (2010). Tabulated for 10-50 wt% ethanol over -35 to 40 degC. Ethanol is a non-electrolyte, food-adjacent freeze-protection coolant, so it is modelled with CoolProp rather than the Laliberte electrolyte correlation. Each cell sits above the solution's freezing line; cells below it are left blank and the explorer will not interpolate across them. Ethanol is volatile and flammable, so closed handling is assumed. Values are for preliminary design; verify against vendor data for critical service.",
